## 13. Conclusions & Recommendations

This analysis identified several operational areas where targeted 
improvements could meaningfully reduce delivery delays and improve 
customer satisfaction.

**🔴 Critical — Late deliveries are longer than expected**  
6,573 affected orders with an average delay of 10.6 days.  
Action: Review carrier SLAs and strengthen escalation procedures 
for delayed shipments.

**🔴 Critical — Customer satisfaction drops once delays begin**  
Review score decreases from 4.5 to 3.8 after the first day of delay.  
Action: Focus operational targets on minimising late deliveries, 
particularly beyond the promised delivery date.

**🟡 High — Delivery performance varies strongly by region**  
Consistent regional delivery gaps identified across seller states.  
Action: Evaluate regional carrier partnerships in lower-performing 
states rather than applying a single national carrier strategy.

**🟡 High — ML model can flag higher-risk orders at placement**  
Gradient Boosting model achieves AUC of 0.71.  
Action: Use predictive alerts to support proactive customer 
communication and early intervention.

**🟢 Opportunity — November consistently creates capacity pressure**  
Repeated seasonal delivery spikes observed each year.  
Action: Introduce an annual Q3 logistics readiness and capacity 
planning review before peak season begins.

